WEBVTT

1
00:00:14.608 --> 00:00:17.450
Once upon a time, there was a poor woodcutter.

2
00:00:18.331 --> 00:00:20.613
He and his wife lived very simply.

3
00:00:21.494 --> 00:00:24.937
The woodcutter often wished for more money and a better life.

4
00:00:25.858 --> 00:00:27.800
But his wishes never came true.

5
00:00:29.492 --> 00:00:33.194
One afternoon the woodcutter was searching for a tree to cut down.

6
00:00:34.335 --> 00:00:36.997
All the trees looked too big or too small.

7
00:00:37.017 --> 00:00:40.619
"I wish I could find a good tree," he said.

8
00:00:42.080 --> 00:00:45.362
Like magic, he suddenly spotted the perfect one.

9
00:00:45.382 --> 00:00:47.984
"My wish actually came true!"

10
00:00:49.064 --> 00:00:54.828
The woodcutter raised his ax Suddenly a small fairy appeared.

11
00:00:57.472 --> 00:00:59.032
"Stop! Please don't chop down my home."

12
00:00:59.973 --> 00:01:01.313
The woodcutter frowned.

13
00:01:01.333 --> 00:01:03.714
"I need wood to make money.

14
00:01:04.294 --> 00:01:06.775
And all the other trees are too big or too small."

15
00:01:06.795 --> 00:01:09.955
"How about this?"

16
00:01:10.536 --> 00:01:11.396
the fairy said.

17
00:01:11.416 --> 00:01:17.017
"If you leave my tree alone, I will grant you three wishes."

18
00:01:19.318 --> 00:01:21.438
"No, thanks," the woodcutter said.

19
00:01:21.458 --> 00:01:23.639
"My wishes never come true."

20
00:01:23.659 --> 00:01:28.112
"These wishes will come true," the fairy said.

21
00:01:28.132 --> 00:01:32.834
"But if they don't, you may return and chop down my tree."

22
00:01:33.834 --> 00:01:36.515
It was getting late, so the woodcutter agreed.

23
00:01:38.595 --> 00:01:42.776
When he arrived home, he told his wife about the fairy and the wishes.

24
00:01:42.796 --> 00:01:46.237
"Ridiculous!" she said.

25
00:01:46.257 --> 00:01:50.418
"Tomorrow you will go back and chop down that dumb fairy's tree."

26
00:01:52.259 --> 00:01:54.079
She set a bowl in front of him.

27
00:01:54.099 --> 00:01:56.020
"Here, have supper."

28
00:01:56.588 --> 00:01:59.170
The woodcutter looked at his bowl and groaned.

29
00:01:59.190 --> 00:02:01.172
"Plain broth again?

30
00:02:01.192 --> 00:02:03.814
I wish we had some sausages."

31
00:02:04.655 --> 00:02:08.398
Poof! Two plump sausages appeared on the table.

32
00:02:09.339 --> 00:02:11.200
The woodcutter was amazed.

33
00:02:11.220 --> 00:02:13.122
"My wish came true!"

34
00:02:13.142 --> 00:02:15.043
"Indeed, it did!"

35
00:02:15.844 --> 00:02:17.005
His wife laughed.

36
00:02:17.025 --> 00:02:21.609
"But you used up a wish on sausages.

37
00:02:22.029 --> 00:02:22.950
How silly!"

38
00:02:22.970 --> 00:02:24.992
The woodcutter frowned.

39
00:02:25.620 --> 00:02:26.561
"It's not funny!

40
00:02:27.382 --> 00:02:30.404
Why, I wish these sausages were stuck in your nose!"

41
00:02:31.285 --> 00:02:34.788
Poof! Now it was the woodcutter's turn to laugh.

42
00:02:37.350 --> 00:02:40.513
The sausages were stuck in his wife's nose!

43
00:02:41.534 --> 00:02:43.235
"Stop laughing!"

44
00:02:43.295 --> 00:02:44.116
she snapped.

45
00:02:44.216 --> 00:02:46.138
"I wish—" "No!"

46
00:02:46.518 --> 00:02:47.659
the woodcutter cried.

47
00:02:47.679 --> 00:02:49.901
"Don't! There's only one wish left.

48
00:02:50.422 --> 00:02:52.904
Let's try to get these sausages out of your nose first."

49
00:02:54.072 --> 00:02:58.274
The woodcutter's wife pulled on a sausage, but it was stuck tightly.

50
00:02:58.294 --> 00:02:59.735
"Let me try."

51
00:03:00.375 --> 00:03:02.976
The woodcutter slowly pulled on a sausage.

52
00:03:02.996 --> 00:03:05.437
"Ow! Stop!

53
00:03:05.537 --> 00:03:06.598
It hurts!"

54
00:03:07.258 --> 00:03:08.418
The woodcutter let go.

55
00:03:08.438 --> 00:03:10.739
"Let's put some grease on the sausages.

56
00:03:11.140 --> 00:03:12.360
Then they'll slide out easily."

57
00:03:13.841 --> 00:03:15.782
He spread some butter on the sausages.

58
00:03:16.702 --> 00:03:17.962
He tried to pull again.

59
00:03:17.982 --> 00:03:21.164
"Ouch!" his wife cried.

60
00:03:21.780 --> 00:03:23.881
"It's not working."

61
00:03:24.401 --> 00:03:25.142
"What should we do?"

62
00:03:25.622 --> 00:03:26.722
the woodcutter asked.

63
00:03:26.742 --> 00:03:30.904
"We still have one wish left," his wife said.

64
00:03:30.924 --> 00:03:36.946
"And I can't live with sausages in my nose."

65
00:03:36.967 --> 00:03:38.327
"You're right.

66
00:03:39.307 --> 00:03:42.829
I wish The woodcutter took a deep breath.

67
00:03:43.689 --> 00:03:45.550
"The sausages were out of my wife's nose!"

68
00:03:46.410 --> 00:03:49.552
Poof! The sausages lay on the table again.

69
00:03:50.936 --> 00:03:53.477
The woodcutter and his wife looked at them sadly.

70
00:03:53.497 --> 00:03:57.138
"We wasted the wishes," the woodcutter said.

71
00:03:57.158 --> 00:04:02.139
"At least the sausages are out of my nose," his wife said.

72
00:04:02.679 --> 00:04:03.680
Then she smiled.

73
00:04:03.700 --> 00:04:07.701
"And you did wish for sausages with supper!"

74
00:04:08.561 --> 00:04:09.961
She began to laugh again.

75
00:04:15.423 --> 00:04:16.223
not eating those!

76
00:04:16.803 --> 00:04:17.763
They were in your nose."

77
00:04:18.284 --> 00:04:19.624
The woodcutter laughed too.

78
00:04:25.131 --> 00:04:28.015
They were no better off than they had been before.

79
00:04:28.856 --> 00:04:33.082
But their three ridiculous wishes sure made them laugh.
